tre of the well ($y = z = 0$) at the moment $\\eta = L$, where $a = 1$, beside Friedmann's universe of the same dust with no well.","clip":"We draw $K\\,L^4$ on a linear scale from $200$ to $400$, with every value inside the panel.","legend":[["line","K","$K$, the Kretschmann scalar"],["line","reference","Friedmann's universe of the same dust with no well"]]},"ricci_scalar":{"opening":"The Ricci scalar $R$ of the universe along the line through the centre of the well ($y = z = 0$) at the moment $\\eta = L$, where $a = 1$, beside Friedmann's universe of the same dust with no well.","clip":"We draw $R\\,L^2$ on a linear scale from $10$ to $16$, with every value inside the panel.","legend":[["line","R","$R$, the Ricci scalar"],["line","reference","Friedmann's universe of the same dust with no well"]]}},"settings":"$L = 1$, the width of the well and the unit of length, at $\\eta = L$ with $|x| \\le 3L$.","input":"A flat universe of dust, $a = \\eta^2/L^2$, with one well of width $L$ held still in comoving coordinates, $\\Phi = \\Psi = -\\tfrac{1}{10}e^{-(x^2 + y^2 + z^2)/L^2}$; in the matter era the potentials of a growing perturbation do not change with time.","clip":"We draw $K\\,L^4$ on a linear scale from $200$ to $400$, with every value inside the panel. We draw $R\\,L^2$ on a linear scale from $10$ to $16$, with every value inside the panel."}]}
